    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "obstacleGrid = [[0,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,0]]  ->  2\nobstacleGrid = [[0,1],[0,0]]              ->  1\nobstacleGrid = [[1]]                      ->  0   (the start is blocked)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: obstacles contribute zero"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Same recurrence as Unique Paths — paths from above plus paths from the left — with one rule: a blocked cell has **0** paths. That also fixes the edges automatically: along the top row, once a cell is blocked, every cell after it has 0 paths, because the only way in was through the obstacle. If the start itself is blocked, the answer is 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Recursion with memoization"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function uniquePathsWithObstacles(grid) {\n  const m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;\n  const memo = new Map();\n  const paths = (r, c) => {\n    if (r < 0 || c < 0 || grid[r][c] === 1) return 0;    // off the grid or blocked\n    if (r === 0 && c === 0) return 1;\n    const key = r * n + c;\n    if (!memo.has(key)) memo.set(key, paths(r - 1, c) + paths(r, c - 1));\n    return memo.get(key);\n  };\n  return paths(m - 1, n - 1);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from functools import cache\n\ndef unique_paths_with_obstacles(grid):\n    @cache\n    def paths(r, c):\n        if r < 0 or c < 0 or grid[r][c] == 1:\n            return 0                      # off the grid or blocked\n        if r == 0 and c == 0:\n            return 1\n        return paths(r - 1, c) + paths(r, c - 1)\n    return paths(len(grid) - 1, len(grid[0]) - 1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "Integer[][] memo;\n\nint uniquePathsWithObstacles(int[][] grid) {\n    memo = new Integer[grid.length][grid[0].length];\n    return paths(grid, grid.length - 1, grid[0].length - 1);\n}\n\nint paths(int[][] grid, int r, int c) {\n    if (r < 0 || c < 0 || grid[r][c] == 1) return 0;     // off the grid or blocked\n    if (r == 0 && c == 0) return 1;\n    if (memo[r][c] != null) return memo[r][c];\n    return memo[r][c] = paths(grid, r - 1, c) + paths(grid, r, c - 1);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int paths(vector<vector<int>>& grid, vector<vector<int>>& memo, int r, int c) {\n    if (r < 0 || c < 0 || grid[r][c] == 1) return 0;     // off the grid or blocked\n    if (r == 0 && c == 0) return 1;\n    if (memo[r][c] != -1) return memo[r][c];\n    return memo[r][c] = paths(grid, memo, r - 1, c) + paths(grid, memo, r, c - 1);\n}\n\nint uniquePathsWithObstacles(vector<vector<int>>& grid) {\n    vector<vector<int>> memo(grid.size(), vector<int>(grid[0].size(), -1));\n    return paths(grid, memo, grid.size() - 1, grid[0].size() - 1);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(m · n), space O(m · n).**"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. A table"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "unique-paths-obstacles",
      "caption": "Open cells add the paths from above and from the left; blocked cells stay at 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function uniquePathsWithObstacles(grid) {\n  const m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;\n  const paths = Array.from({ length: m }, () => new Array(n).fill(0));\n  for (let r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n      if (grid[r][c] === 1) continue;                     // blocked: 0 paths\n      if (r === 0 && c === 0) { paths[r][c] = 1; continue; }\n      paths[r][c] = (r > 0 ? paths[r - 1][c] : 0) + (c > 0 ? paths[r][c - 1] : 0);   // above + left\n    }\n  }\n  return paths[m - 1][n - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def unique_paths_with_obstacles(grid):\n    m, n = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    paths = [[0] * n for _ in range(m)]\n    for r in range(m):\n        for c in range(n):\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                continue                  # blocked: 0 paths\n            if r == 0 and c == 0:\n                paths[r][c] = 1\n                continue\n            paths[r][c] = (paths[r - 1][c] if r > 0 else 0) + (paths[r][c - 1] if c > 0 else 0)   # above + left\n    return paths[m - 1][n - 1]"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int uniquePathsWithObstacles(int[][] grid) {\n    int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;\n    int[][] paths = new int[m][n];\n    for (int r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n            if (grid[r][c] == 1) continue;               // blocked: 0 paths\n            if (r == 0 && c == 0) { paths[r][c] = 1; continue; }\n            paths[r][c] = (r > 0 ? paths[r - 1][c] : 0) + (c > 0 ? paths[r][c - 1] : 0);   // above + left\n        }\n    }\n    return paths[m - 1][n - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int uniquePathsWithObstacles(vector<vector<int>>& grid) {\n    int m = grid.size(), n = grid[0].size();\n    vector<vector<int>> paths(m, vector<int>(n, 0));\n    for (int r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n            if (grid[r][c] == 1) continue;               // blocked: 0 paths\n            if (r == 0 && c == 0) { paths[r][c] = 1; continue; }\n            paths[r][c] = (r > 0 ? paths[r - 1][c] : 0) + (c > 0 ? paths[r][c - 1] : 0);   // above + left\n        }\n    }\n    return paths[m - 1][n - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(m · n), space O(m · n).**"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. One row"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function uniquePathsWithObstacles(grid) {\n  const n = grid[0].length;\n  const row = new Array(n).fill(0);\n  row[0] = 1;                                            // the start (if open)\n  for (const cells of grid) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n      if (cells[c] === 1) row[c] = 0;                    // blocked\n      else if (c > 0) row[c] += row[c - 1];              // above (old row[c]) + left\n    }\n  }\n  return row[n - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def unique_paths_with_obstacles(grid):\n    n = len(grid[0])\n    row = [0] * n\n    row[0] = 1                            # the start (if open)\n    for cells in grid:\n        for c in range(n):\n            if cells[c] == 1:\n                row[c] = 0                # blocked\n            elif c > 0:\n                row[c] += row[c - 1]      # above (old row[c]) + left\n    return row[n - 1]"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int uniquePathsWithObstacles(int[][] grid) {\n    int n = grid[0].length;\n    int[] row = new int[n];\n    row[0] = 1;                                          // the start (if open)\n    for (int[] cells : grid) {\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n            if (cells[c] == 1) row[c] = 0;               // blocked\n            else if (c > 0) row[c] += row[c - 1];        // above (old row[c]) + left\n        }\n    }\n    return row[n - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int uniquePathsWithObstacles(vector<vector<int>>& grid) {\n    int n = grid[0].size();\n    vector<long long> row(n, 0);\n    row[0] = 1;                                          // the start (if open)\n    for (auto& cells : grid) {\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n            if (cells[c] == 1) row[c] = 0;               // blocked\n            else if (c > 0) row[c] += row[c - 1];        // above (old row[c]) + left\n        }\n    }\n    return (int)row[n - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(m · n), space O(n).** A blocked start sets `row[0] = 0` on the first row, and it stays 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Recursion with memoization",
          "time": "O(m · n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each **cell** is solved once from above and the left.",
          "space": "O(m · n)",
          "spaceWhy": "One memo entry **per cell**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "A table",
          "time": "O(m · n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each cell is filled **once**; obstacles add zero.",
          "space": "O(m · n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The **full grid** of counts."
        },
        {
          "approach": "One row",
          "time": "O(m · n)",
          "timeWhy": "The **same cells**, row by row.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "Each row only needs **the row above**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**The start or the end is blocked** — 0.",
        "**An obstacle on the top row** — every cell to its right on that row has 0 paths.",
        "**A single open cell** — 1.",
        "**A wall of obstacles** — 0 paths."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
